---
title: "7 · Duplicate, void and delete a draft"
description: Copy an invoice into a new draft, cancel an issued invoice with a reason, and delete a draft.
sidebar:
  order: 8
  label: "7 · Duplicate, void and delete a draft"
---

## Duplicate an invoice

**Who:** any member who can see the invoice.

Use this for a similar invoice, for example next month's retainer, or to reissue an invoice that was voided.

{% steps %}

1. Open the invoice and select **More** › **Duplicate invoice**.
2. A new draft opens in the editor with the same client, lines and layout. It has no number, and no payment or history is copied.
3. Change what is needed, select **Update**, and issue it when it is ready.

{% /steps %}

Any invoice can be duplicated, whatever its status. Uploaded invoices and credit notes cannot be duplicated.

## Void an invoice

**Who:** managers and tenant admins.

Voiding cancels an issued invoice. The invoice keeps its number, which is never given to another invoice, so the numbering has no gap.

{% steps %}

1. Open the invoice and select **More** › **Void invoice**.
2. Enter the **Reason**. **Void invoice** stays greyed out until a reason is entered.
3. Select **Void invoice**.

{% /steps %}

The status becomes **Void** and the reason is shown on the invoice page and in its history. The online link stops working, and the PDF is produced again with a VOID mark. A void invoice cannot be changed any more.

An invoice with a payment or applied credit cannot be voided. First delete its payments and remove the applied credit (see [Record payments](/en/invoices/payments/) and [Credit notes](/en/invoices/credit-notes/)), then void it. A credit note is voided in the same way, with **Void credit note**.

{% aside type="tip" title="Wrong issuing entity" %}
The issuing entity of an issued invoice cannot be changed, because its number belongs to that entity's series. Void the invoice, duplicate it, correct the duplicate and issue it again.
{% /aside %}

## Delete a draft

**Who:** any member who can see the invoice. Credit note drafts are deleted by managers.

Open the draft, select **More** › **Delete draft** and confirm. The draft is removed. It had no number, so nothing is skipped in the numbering. Only drafts can be deleted; an issued invoice can only be voided.
